th `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C41-N01 tree, tabs, request line, response pane, history; C41-N02 Send by keyboard with the announced completion; C41-N03 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_api` (the C33 immutable-history tests move or stay registered); Vitest `v2/workbench/api-client.test.tsx`.\n# C42 — Academy\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C41.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\nR2App `start=academy`. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nthe prototype's page chrome (title row, 1.4fr/1fr frame, Learning-paths row) around the hosted learner embed with the Rust-owned theme; the composite is judged on the chrome, the embed's content is the Academy's own (P19).\n\n## Core it reads\n\n`ShellSnapshot.academy`, `learner`, `academyOrigin`, `academyOffline`. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C42/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C42-N01 chrome and embed mounted with the theme; C42-N02 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_academy`; Vitest `v2/academy.test.tsx`.\n# C43 — Wizard re-port\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C42.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\nR2Onboard, every `step`, `filled`, `verify`, `mode=add`. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nthe presentation re-ported over the existing state machine and intents: 320px rail (244px in add mode) with brand tile, numbered steps, done checks, Optional/Skipped tags, privacy note and theme button; a pinned footer (Cancel in add mode, Back, hint, Step n of m, Skip, primary); section cards (18/20), a 2-column field grid, segmented control, switch; each step's layout per the board; the add sheet at a fixed 1160×780 without the modal's padding. Model-driven extras (credential save/remove forms, workspace chooser, unavailable products) housed inside the prototype's cards.\n\n## Core it reads\n\n`ShellSnapshot.setup`; the setup intents of C29 unchanged. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C43/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C43-N01 every step first-run; C43-N02 the add sheet; C43-N03 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_wizard` (C29's `ui_v2_onboarding` stays registered); Vitest `v2/wizard/*.test.tsx`.\n# C44 — Legacy shell removal, P09 closure\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C43.\n\nD060 (2026-10-31): the alpha import (C23's Import from v1 destination, view, wizard box and first-run frame) is removed in this chunk; C23's native checks are retired and the cumulative set drops `acceptance_c23.py`.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\n—. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nmap every assertion in the legacy native acceptance scripts to its replacement driver and native-check id (`legacy-script-map.md` under the chunk evidence); remove the legacy shell, its feature-view switch, the `ui_variant` flag, the legacy feature components no v2 screen imports, and the legacy scripts, in one commit on a branch merged after review; cumulative native acceptance of every destination and the whole-app screenshot set; every C28–C43 chunk accepted at 8 raised to 9; the P09 phase review at 9 (the C29 live Vulture row must have run).\n\n## Core it reads\n\n—. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C44/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C44-N01 cumulative acceptance of every destination), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_closure`.\n\n## The workspace key on the one presentation\n\nThe legacy AI Gateway view's Playground held the form that saved a workspace's inference key (C18); with that view gone, the first-run wizard's tenant step saves the key and the Gateway card's Workspaces tab holds the same form for the chosen workspace (`data-slot=\"gateway-workspace-key\"`: Inference endpoint, Workspace inference key, Save or Replace workspace key, Remove workspace key; the key's Keychain state from the tenant's snapshot; the field is emptied as soon as the secret is sent). The Harness's missing-key text and the wizard's hint name that tab. Found by the cumulative run of the C38 driver, whose setup now saves the key there.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 independent review verdict\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"request_id\",\n    \"attempt_id\",\n    \"subject\",\n    \"fingerprints\",\n    \"scores\",\n    \"required_fixes\",\n    \"blockers\",\n    \"evidence_gaps\",\n    \"optional_suggestions\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"inspected_files\",\n    \"recommendation\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"request_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"attempt_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Chunk C01-C44 or phase P01-P09 under review\"\n    },\n    \"fingerprints\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"source\",\n        \"dependencies\",\n        \"build_flags\",\n        \"evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"source\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"dependencies\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"build_flags\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"evidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"scores\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"architecture\",\n        \"behavior\",\n        \"authority_security\",\n        \"validation\",\n        \"overall\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"architecture\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"behavior\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"authority_security\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"validation\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"overall\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required_fixes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"blockers\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"evidence_gaps\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"optional_suggestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"limitations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"inspected_files\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"recommendation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"pass\",\n        \"fail\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\nCOMMANDS [\n  {\n    \"record\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/runs/run-attempt-10.json\",\n    \"subject\": \"P09\",\n    \"attempt\": \"attempt-10\",\n    \"time\": \"2026-11-02T19:56:44+0000\",\n    \"cwd\": \"/Users/cdot/development/redtail/prisma-airs-desktop-v2-current\",\n    \"toolchain\": {\n      \"rustc\": \"rustc 1.99.0 (b940084d7 2026-09-28)\",\n      \"cargo\": \"cargo 1.99.0 (5f94df478 2026-08-27)\",\n      \"node\": \"v24.21.0\",\n      \"pnpm\": \"10.6.5\",\n      \"rustup_active\": \"1.99.0-aarch64-apple-darwin (overr