me … | exercised | C37-N02 — Tab from Read now reaches the tabs and rows; Enter opens a row's detail | C37-N02 pass |\n| C31-N01 | Administration renders the core's inventory: Agentic Identity and Endpoint Security show their gate and nothing else; each tab offers exactly its admitted actions with… | exercised | C39-N01 — the inventory per tab with exactly its admitted actions; the gated products show their gate | C39-N01 pass |\n| C31-N02 | A custom topic edit opens the review sheet; Apply stays disabled until the typed name matches exactly (empty and wrong case refused); Apply opens the native confirmati… | self-run | C31-N02, C39-N02 — acceptance_c31.py through legacy_v2: the custom topic edit through the review sheet, Apply on the exact name, the native confirmation, applied once; C39-N02 asserts the same on the board | C31-N02 pass, C39-N02 pass |\n| C31-N03 | The staged Runtime key rotation: 'Issue additional key…' reviewed with CREATE and confirmed natively issues one key and shows 'Additional key issued · old key still ac… | self-run | C31-N03 — acceptance_c31.py through legacy_v2: Issue additional key… reviewed and confirmed natively, the issued key revealed through the host's secret sheet, the review exit, the Inbox reminder and its resumption, the old key's removal (invariants I6/I7) | C31-N03 pass |\n| C31-N04 | The accessibility additions (DESIGN-V2 §8) on the changed UI: the review sheet is the one topmost modal (the rail hidden beneath it) and Escape closes it with focus re… | exercised | C39-N02 — the review sheet docked with Close review and Done | C39-N02 pass |\n| C32-N01 | The Harness renders in the v2 shell on the existing engine: the title row names the tenant, the engine and the workspace; the prerequisites checklist is hidden once sa… | exercised | C38-N01 — the title band names tenant, engine and workspace; a fresh tenant's first send starts a conversation | C38-N01 pass |\n| C32-N02 | A command the engine asks to run while the project is read-only is decided in the page (Approve once / Decline) after a project is chosen through the embedded project … | exercised | C38-N01, C38-N02, C38-N03 — a decision held in the aside; Approve once / Decline; a tenant switch while it waits meets the guard | C38-N01 pass, C38-N02 pass, C38-N03 pass |\n| C32-N03 | The workspace MCP catalog read the engine asks for (airs_desktop.mcpServers) is shown as read-only and read only once approved in the page; a change the engine propose… | exercised | C38-N01 — the mcpServers read waits, is approved in the page and made once | C38-N01 pass |\n| C32-N04 | Keyboard: Tab from the message box reaches Send or End; at the 900×600 minimum and 200% zoom in both themes nothing on the Harness screen lies past the window's right … | exercised | C38-N02 — Tab from the message box; 900×600 at 200% without horizontal scroll | C38-N02 pass |\n| C33-N01 | Test Cases in the v2 shell: Add starter packs lists the tenant's starter cases with their pack name and Not run; the product filter and search narrow the rows; a non-R… | exercised | C40-N01 — the starter packs with Not run; the product filter and search; Inspect for a non-Runtime case | C40-N01 pass |\n| C33-N02 | API Client in the v2 shell: Send announces \"<request> · <code> · <duration>\" in a status region with the response body outside it (known gap 5, V2-T14); after a topic … | exercised | C41-N01 — Send announces request · code · duration in the status region with the body outside it; History keeps both runs | C41-N01 pass |\n| C33-N03 | Show the calls: hidden by default once a tenant exists; while chosen, a panel beside the destination lists the calls made for the tenant (the scan's request line and i… | exercised | C35-N01, C36-N01, C40-N01 — the Explain switch shows and hides the calls panel and the Explain banner | C35-N01 pass, C36-N01 pass, C40-N01 pass |\n| C33-N04 | Keyboard and layout on both screens (T09): Test Cases' search and product filter in Tab order with the focus ring on a changed control; the API Client's Send reached b… | exercised | C40-N02, C41-N02 — the two screens' keyboard and layout matrices | C40-N02 pass, C41-N02 pass |\n| C33-N05 | The library's workflows in the v2 Test Cases (C12 parity): a Runtime case and a specification created through the form, a case removed, an export saved, cancelled and … | exercised | C40-N01 — a case and a specification saved, a case removed, Export… saved and cancelled, the exported file imported, a case copied to another tenant | C40-N01 pass |\n\n## What the legacy shell asserted and where it lives now\n\n- **The shell itself** (C01 rail, topbar, palette, Settings tabs): C35 (`acceptance_c35.py`, C35-N01..N03) and C44-N01.\n- **Settings' \"Use the new interface\" switch** (C28, C35): removed; C44-N01 asserts its absence. The core accepts `setUiVariant` and ignores it (`ui_v2_closure`).\n- **Runtime Security, AI Gateway, Red Team & Models as pages** (C03, C09, C10, C13, C16–C18): Administration's product cards (C39); the Go/palette entries open the product in Administration (`ui_v2_closure`, C44-N01).\n- **Sessions & Reports** (C11) and **Import from v1** (C23): framed by the v2 shell as before; no board of their own in P09. C44-N01 opens each.\n- **The Academy destination** (C04–C07): the v2 Academy chrome around the same learner pages (C42); the learner suites under `features/academy/*.test.tsx` now exercise the v2 component.\n- **The API Client** (C14, C15) and **the Library** (C12): C41 and C40.\n- **The Harness** (C19–C22): C38.\n- **Privacy, diagnostics and network** (C24): C44-N01 repeats the no-plaintext-secret sweep over the whole-app capture set.\n\n## Files removed in C44\n\n`apps/desktop/src/shell/desktop-shell.tsx` (+test), `command-palette.tsx`, `icons.ts`; `features/academy/academy-view.tsx` (+test), `features/administration/administration-view.tsx`, `features/red-team/red-team-view.tsx` (+test), `features/runtime/runtime-view.tsx`, `features/runtime/overview-inbox.tsx` (+test); the `Interface` fieldset of Settings; the legacy branch of `app.tsx` and `feature-body.tsx`.\n\n## Legacy suites retired with the shell, and the two that run again on the one presentation\n\n`features/administration/administration-view.test.tsx` (the legacy Administration view's inventories: the v2 Administration suite covers paging, denied refresh, context replacement, the review sheet and the inventories through the v2 imports). The DLP authoring suite is ported, assertion for assertion, to `v2/admin/dlp-authoring.test.tsx` (the Runtime card's DLP tab and its inventory radios; the review sheet hosts the change workbench): v1's actions per inventory, the dictionary draft from typed keywords, a chosen file by its token only, the whole-list replace on edit, typed keywords kept when a choice is cancelled or fails, and metadata that must be one JSON object. The management-client onboarding suite (the owner's uncommitted `features/tenants/management-credential.test.tsx`, excluded) is ported to `v2/settings/management-credential.test.tsx`: the secret cleared before awaiting and kept out of storage, the required fields, the TSG requirement, the SSO pointer, verification as one management read with faithful failures, and removal of the management client only.\n\n## Files kept although no v2 screen imports them\n\nThe owner's uncommitted work (docs/planning/evidence/C28/owner-work.json) touches `features/gateway/gateway-view.tsx`, `playground.tsx`, `features/harness/harness-view.tsx`, `sign-in-panel.tsx`, `prerequisites.tsx`, `features/library/library-view.tsx`, `features/workbench/workbench-view.tsx` and their tests; deleting them on this branch would collide with that work, so they and the components only they import (`gateway-files.tsx`, `gateway-observe.tsx`, the Harness panels, `document-editor.tsx`, `request-send.tsx`) stay as unreferenced code until the owner's work lands. Their tests still run.\n\n## C39a attempt-01 remediation carried in C44\n\n- R1: below 760 CSS px the inventory rows stack their cells (`tokens.css`), and `acceptance_c39.py`'s layout predicate fails on any two texts of the table drawn over each other, beyond containment.\n- R2: Close details retires the read in flight and the opened item (`inventory-table.tsx`); a regression test keeps the panel closed and focus stable after a late reply and a later refresh.\n- R3: the empty search says it searched the page that was read and points at First page / Next page (`copy.ts`); a two-page regression test with the match on the other page.\n- E2: `administration.test.tsx` adds the v2 Playground's submit (refused, unconfirmed, admitted), cancel and save-case handlers and the table's paging, denied refresh and context replacement through the v2 imports.\n{\n  \"schema\": \"airs-v2/p09-native-build-inputs/1\",\n  \"generation\": \"worf-10-c32-scoped-confirmation\",\n  \"source_head\": \"2bb87b9b530c255d0e9d34609a97b70b347dae95\",\n  \"worktree_diff\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/preparations/worf-10-c32-scoped-confirmation/fixture-remediation.diff\",\n  \"worktree_diff_sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n  \"prepare\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-prepare.json\",\n  \"prepare_sha256\": \"27b0465c9f13318061a8944e074557399f1353e5db26da4f227f9b94f755e4f8\",\n  \"executable_sha256\": \"d8bf6a0f91507b6643a9888169873fe5c8bc1c96739bc2cd33b61aa3805ebcca\",\n  \"bundle_sha256\": \"41dbaa58a2d9a8e02918faa0da07657d1987e6bf96e99587b89687ebf9060aab\",\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"procedure\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/runs/hash-inputs.sh\",\n    \"procedure_sha256\": \"0a4f9546e1aa4a812da6a946c6ee73d9a0e69c3fd4534dd3d480d5c804b53ea1\",\n    \"before_inventory\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/preparations/worf-10-c32-scoped-confirmation/inputs-before.sha256\",\n    \"after_inventory\": \"docs/planning/evidence/P09/preparations/worf-10-c32-scoped-confirmation/inputs-after.sha256\",\n    \"before_digest\": \"b35a8d04c49e040dd8cc