nstalled-release behavior is outside this verdict.\",\n    \"The revocable presentation owner now travels from configuration review/result admission through native effect execution, queued presentation and explicit copy permission. Inspected the production Host/IPC regressions and original reload and queued-presentation red/green evidence. Current retained logs report all ten lifecycle cases passing. I did not independently reproduce AppKit scheduling races or run a fresh Rust suite.\",\n    \"Verified required evidence, preparation, executable, driver and controller bindings across all 19 current native drivers. C31-N01\\u2013N04 and C39-N01\\u2013N04 pass on the current bundle. The unrelated superseded raw C24-N06 failure remains preserved rather than relabeled.\",\n    \"Read retained AX trees and representative captures. Both Gateway key kinds now reach successful details with Edit, Rotate, Remove and Close details, without Runtime staged-rotation actions. Independently ran all 12 read-only administration coverage tests successfully. Native interaction and spoken VoiceOver output were not independently exercised here.\",\n    \"Retained current logs report 550 renderer tests, 15 ui_v2_reviews tests and the host regressions passing. Inspected production-interface tests cover typed review binding, tenant retirement, delayed settlement, unknown outcomes, reconciliation, durable rotation facts and stable timestamps; passing counts alone were not treated as behavioral proof.\",\n    \"Verified C30's exact raw verdict, request, receipt, audit and owner-decision bindings. C30 remains owner-complete with its independent 9/9/9/8/8 fail verdict and closed findings unchanged; those findings were not reopened. C29's actual full-nine G7 review and C41's separate exception remain historical standing.\",\n    \"C31 topic create/apply/readback/cleanup receipts are historical live evidence for their recorded inputs, not a fresh live run of G9. Historical C30 timing likewise establishes no current performance measurement. L19 retains three charged reads and zero remaining allowance.\",\n    \"No application files were changed, endpoints called, real credentials accessed or OS permissions granted. C26/P08 controller and release gates remain separate. The read-only sandbox prevents writing the designated artifact; this returned JSON is the verdict.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [\n    \"Retained nonrequired presentation note: apps/desktop/src/v2/admin/review-sheet.tsx displays Draft for issued and completed rotations although the rotation panel reports the correct stage. Deriving that pill from RotationView.stage would remove the inconsistency; this does not require another C31 cycle.\"\n  ]\n}\ndocs/planning/reviews/C32/attempt-23/verdict-returned.json\n{\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Verified all 8,242 scoped file hashes, complete compiled-input membership and 18,348 hashes, matching before/after inventories, build flags and all 18 check-log hashes. Hash consistency does not authenticate compiler execution or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Verified the sealed source transition, current executable, complete bundle including executable modes and symlink targets, six frozen prototype files and bundled Harness engine pin. The reviewed G10 qualification uses aarch64-apple-darwin and test-fixtures; signed installed-release acceptance is separate.\",\n    \"The C32 fix carries admission-time revocable ownership through ConfirmHarness into confirm_scoped, revokes before dismissal and retains private settlement revalidation. Inspected both production-interface race regressions and native Cancel/Allow controls. Retained current logs report all eight Harness integration tests passing; I did not independently rerun Rust, renderer or GUI suites.\",\n    \"The original loopback old-red log records both intended stale-sheet assertion failures. The separate sandbox bind failures and initial green-build borrow-check failure remain distinguishable. No contemporaneous complete old-red worktree seal exists; that historical limitation does not establish an exact fully hashed old-red snapshot.\",\n    \"Verified bindings and required passing evidence across all 20 current native drivers. Read C32/C38 acceptance records, retained AX trees and representative captures covering project selection, approvals, switch guards, proposal review, ending, keyboard access, zoom and Reduce Motion. The superseded raw C24-N06 failure remains preserved.\",\n    \"Native evidence uses the real pinned engine with synthetic services, fixture folder selection and WKWebView captures. Native interactions, AppKit scheduling and spoken VoiceOver output were not independently exercised in this review.\",\n    \"Independently ran 21 read-only tests successfully: four Harness source-boundary tests, five C32 coverage-contract tests and twelve administration coverage tests. Current Gateway detail AX trees show successful scoped service/user-key details with Edit, Rotate, Remove and Close details; failed or loading panels cannot satisfy that evidence contract.\",\n    \"Verified C31 attempt-07's actual all-nine verdict, receipt, audit and preserved original scope. The shared-authority projection limits current differences to declared C32 Harness branches. The final C31 review cap was honored; no owner override activation or additional C31 review was inferred.\",\n    \"C30 remains owner-complete under its exact exception, with its independent 9/9/9/8/8 fail verdict and closed findings unchanged. G9, C29 live qualification and C30 timing remain historical. L19 retains three charged reads and zero remaining allowance; C26/P08 and release gates remain separate.\",\n    \"No application files were changed, endpoints called, real credentials accessed or OS permissions granted. The read-only sandbox prevents the designated artifact write; this returned JSON is the verdict.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": []\n}\ndocs/planning/reviews/C44/attempt-05/verdict-returned.json\n{\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"This verdict covers the scoped C44 implementation at 31169c2b9fae7a226b5d18c6665f02b883f83370, including the collection-scope and render-time retirement corrections. Unrelated owner work and predecessor-only merged implementation are outside this verdict. C43 attempt-02 has a matching passing verdict and its reviewed commit is an ancestor of this tree.\",\n    \"All four supplied fingerprints reproduced. All 1,141 scoped file hashes, 18,389 listed build/test input hashes, unchanged before/after inventories, 16 run-log hashes, native-record hashes, executable hash and 1,621-entry prepared bundle hash matched. Scoped and compiled inputs still matched after the independent probes; the current attempt's review outputs are excluded from its source inventory.\",\n    \"Independently ran the retained ui_v2_closure binary: 3 passed. Independent in-memory probes of the production ApiClient and RequestEditor passed all three collection-replacement cases, including identical collection IDs and basenames, every committed DOM and a delayed old reply. The current-checkout parser accepted a valid scope and rejected five missing, malformed or path-shaped scopes. These probes used synthetic dispatch/observation, no network and no file writes.\",\n    \"Broader validation relies on hash-verified retained logs: 535 desktop tests, the separate truth test, 745 fixture-enabled desktop-core tests with one ignored test, 46 host tests and the recorded formatting, lint, binding, typecheck, controller and build checks passed. No flake-retry logs are present for attempt-05. Full suites and builds were not independently rerun.\",\n    \"Native validation relies on retained observations, AX trees and captures, including 13 closure trees, the Harness switch guard, rotation workflow and four whole-app screenshots. All 300 legacy assertion IDs match the manifest; every exercised, self-run or ported target passes on the prepared executable. The owner's record accepts the 88 remaining retirements. C24-N06 and C31-N01/N04 retain superseded failures; missing C24 aggregate references belong to that superseded check. Retired assertions are not represented as native passes.\",\n    \"Native automation, spoken VoiceOver and live-product qualification were not independently performed. Parity approval and retirement acceptance are repository-recorded owner evidence, not independently authenticated. The packet discloses the lost original attempt-03 verdict and recovery of the overwritten attempt-04 artifacts; this review does not reconstruct the lost verdict.\",\n    \"This implementation pass does not complete P09 or certify release readiness. Controller receipts, remaining phase-wide remediation to 9, C29 live Vulture qualification, related re-reviews and the P09 phase review remain separate obligations. D060's deferred import-contract removal and product rename remain outside this chunk.\",\n    \"The reviewer is a separate read-only Codex session within the current implementer's model family. No application source was changed, product endpoint called or real credential accessed. The atomic verdict write failed with PermissionError in the read-only sandbox; the controller must persist this returned JSON.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [\n    \"Refresh stale Import from v1 descriptions in apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-body.tsx, tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c44.py and docs/planning/evidence/C44/parity/notes.md to reflect D060.\",\n    \"For future native runs, record the actual orchestrator instead of the drivers' hard-coded historical performed_by attribution. This packet explicitly discloses that discrepancy.\"\n  ]\n}\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/native/cumulative/C38/native-acceptance.json ['schema', 'subject', 'recorded_utc', 'method', 'performed_by', 'host', 'app', 'checks', 'limitations', 'screens']\n{\n  \"schema\": \"airs-v2/native-acceptance/1\",\n  \"subject\": \"C38\",\n  \"recorded_utc\": \"2